## Context
Exposed by the sixth smelt (2026-11-01), page
`memory/topics/skills-docs-and-hooks.md` open questions. Flagged earlier by
PR #1975 (closed unmerged) as one of three conflicts awaiting the author.

Claim A: `rules/workflow.md` § Severity floor — file a ticket only when the
defect "blocks a merge, corrupts state, or bites the science".

Claim B: `skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md` § Complaint or triage — triage
orders work by "a contradiction that misleads a model into a wrong act
first, then a skill presuming another's ownership, then mechanical lint, then
runtime drift".

Both word a severity floor differently ("bites the science" vs "misleads a
model into a wrong act"); one governs ticket-filing, the other triage
ordering. A memory cannot override a rule; smelt presents neither as settled.

## Question for the author
Which wording is the floor, or are the two scopes (ticket-filing vs triage
ordering) meant to differ? Smelt picks no side and proposes no rule.
